      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "easier moments arrive when you stop comparing your behind-the-scenes struggle to everyone else's highlight reel, shifting focus to tiny, manageable steps rather than the grand finish line. This hard path is not an end state designed for misery, but a grinding process where progress is often invisible until you stand still and look back. Eventually, the sheer weight of the race becomes too heavy to hold so tightly, forcing you to let go of who you think you must be and just breathe through the exhaustion.",
